---
// PDF-16 Phase B (2026-08-31) — re-derived from `uv run pdftooling --help`
// and each example verb's own `--help`. All sixteen pdf-tooling specs have
// now landed, so the Phase A caveat this comment used to carry ("only
// commands that exist in wave 3 ... the entire Commands: block is
// `version`") no longer holds. `merge`, `rotate` and `compress` below are
// real, shipped invocations; every flag used in every example was checked
// against that verb's own `--help` before being written here.
//
// Architectural constraint (backlog B-097): neither `ocr` nor
// `watermark --pages N` appears in any example below, because both also
// modify pages sharing a /Contents object — see PLAN.md §11.1.6. Other
// verbs' page selection (as used by `rotate` here) is unaffected.
//
// PDF-93 D4: the three fake macOS traffic lights are deleted here — they
// were the page's only off-palette colours (E7) — and the chrome bar is
// left in plate-K/M terms: a mono micro label left, quiet meta right. The
// bar's FINAL content (`bash — pdftooling`, `exit 0` with an ink tick) and
// the `{ command, comment }` data-driven grid this transcript becomes are
// PDF-95's, which extracts the shared `Terminal` component this item does
// not build.
const install = `# Install (published on PyPI)
uv tool install pdf-tooling
# or: pip install pdf-tooling`;

const commands = `pdftooling doctor                                                    # which engines resolved, and how
pdftooling merge a.pdf b.pdf -O merged.pdf                           # concatenate PDFs into one file
pdftooling rotate report.pdf --pages 2-4 --angle 90 -O rotated.pdf   # rotate pages 2-4 by 90°
pdftooling compress report.pdf -O small.pdf                          # lossless structural shrink`;
---

